The login page now uses the same markup and styles as `volto-authomatic`, which are the ones Volto's own login form has: a fixed-width card with a titled header, a description strip, labelled fields under a single underline, and submit and cancel as icon buttons on a divided row. Two add-ons that both replace `/login` looking like two different products is a worse outcome than either of them looking like itself.

The panel is a new `LoginPanel` component, and the password form follows `PloneForm`: `@plone/components` `TextField` and `Button`, the `.PloneAuth` class the styles are written against, and `#login-form-submit` / `#login-form-cancel`. `@plone/components` is declared as a peer dependency, as `volto-authomatic` declares it. The ported rules live in `styles.css` rather than a second stylesheet, flattened from the two SCSS files they came from. @ericof
